      "content": "The true gold standard for global professional attire is \"contextual minimalism,\" which prioritizes neutral, high-quality silhouettes over rigid gender norms or specific regional mandates. You should aim for a wardrobe anchored in natural fibers like linen or fine wool, avoided logos, and a dedicated color palette of charcoal, navy, and cream that ensures you look sharp in any business environment. For men, this means a impeccably fitted blazer paired with tailored trousers rather than a stiff suit jacket alone; for women, a structured blouse or silk button-down with a pencil skirt and leather loafers creates the perfect balance of authority and approachability. Ultimately, the look should feel intentional yet unpretentious, conveying that you have studied the local norms while maintaining an international standard of refinement.",
